Bug 2071585 - Prevent POP3 connection attempts and alerts while offline. r=mkmelin

POP3 opens sockets directly, so stop mail checks before creating a client when the application is offline. Reset the biff state when that check fails synchronously.

Correct background error classification so checks without a message window do not show alerts, and cover both behaviors with regression tests.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326015

